ED shipments before allowing cancellation.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added OrderRepository dependency and validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders. Required by the specification.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Added two error codes: `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` (409 when cancelling order with confirmed shipment) and `SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER` (409 when creating shipment for cancelled order). Required for the API contract.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 6 new tests:\n   - `cancels_an_ACTIVE_order_and_returns_200` — Verifies basic cancel works\n   - `cancelled_order_persists` — Verifies persistence\n   - `cancels_CREATED_shipments_when_cancelling_an_order` — Verifies cascade to shipments\n   - `cancel_fails_with_409_if_any_shipment_is_CONFIRMED` — Verifies all-or-nothing with CONFIRMED shipments\n   - `cancelling_an_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_and_changes_nothing` — Verifies idempotency\n   - `cancel_returns_404_for_unknown_order` — Verifies error case\n   Required for acceptance criteria coverage.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 2 new tests:\n   - `rejects_shipment_creation_for_a_cancelled_order_with_409` — Verifies shipment rejection for cancelled orders\n   - `allows_shipment_creation_for_non_existent_order_existing_behavior` — Verifies existing behavior is preserved\n   Required for acceptance criteria coverage.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are covered by tests, all code follows existing patterns, and all cases named in the requirement are implemented.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint to allow cancelling active orders before shipment confirmation, managing order and shipment statuses atomically\nChanged       Order.kt: added OrderStatus enum and status field\n              OrderController.kt: added cancel endpoint with shipment orchestration\n              ShipmentRepository.kt: added findByOrderId method for cascade checking\n              ShipmentController.kt: added validation to reject shipments for cancelled orders\n              ApiError.kt: added ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT and SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt: added 6 comprehensive tests for cancel endpoint\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt: added 2 tests for shipment-cancelled-order interaction\nTests         cancel_active_order_cancels_created_shipments: verifies order status change and shipment cascade\n              cancel_active_order_rejects_confirmed_shipments: verifies 409 conflict and all-or-nothing atomicity\n              cancelling_an_already_cancelled_order_succeeds: verifies idempotent retry behavior\n              cancel_returns_404_for_unknown_order: verifies 404 error case\n              rejects_shipment_creation_for_a_cancelled_order_with_409: verifies shipment creation rejection\n              All existing tests (OrderControllerTest, ShipmentControllerTest, CustomerControllerTest): continue to pass\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test (from sample-service directory)\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS - 21 tests passed, 0 failures, 0 errors\n              Details: 10 OrderControllerTest (6 new), 7 ShipmentControllerTest (2 new), 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests, 3 CustomerControllerTest\nNot done      None - all acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, build successful\n```","ttft_ms":2303,"type":"result","duration_ms":178155,"uuid":"0b288afd-16a8-42a5-9848-c49a49c80886","ttft_stream_ms":630,"time_to_request_ms":32,"first_content_frame_ms":630,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

